# A subscope input bound to a variable that may stay empty — refused

`tussen` is defined only when `pas_toe` holds and is passed to the subscope
`kamer`. Catala raises "no applicable rule to define this variable" at the
argument when `pas_toe` is false, while the callee reads its input as filled
and the IR computes `grondslag + 10` as 10. The plugin refuses the read of
`tussen`. Own-authored, rights-free.

```catala
declaration scope Kamer:
  input grondslag content integer
  output uitkomst content integer

scope Kamer:
  definition uitkomst equals grondslag + 10

declaration scope Aanslag:
  input pas_toe content boolean
  internal tussen content integer
  kamer scope Kamer
  output heffing content integer

scope Aanslag:
  definition tussen under condition pas_toe consequence equals 5
  definition kamer.grondslag equals tussen
  definition heffing equals kamer.uitkomst
```
